{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's heavy riffs, intricate rhythms, and immersive songs.",
    "American Idiot and The Young and the Hopeless connect with the melodic punk side of my listening reflected by Chuck, though I would choose the Tool albums first today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "X&Y and How to Dismantle An Atomic offer melodic rock, but melody alone does not satisfy my current interest in heavier guitars and more intricate rhythms.",
    "Kid A's electronic atmosphere and The Piper at the Gates of Dawn's psychedelia do not offer the particular kind of heaviness I want; hip-hop and polished pop feel even further from that interest."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat a broad interest in rock as enough, even though softer rock, psychedelic rock, and heavy metal appeal to me for different reasons.",
    "The poppier side of my earlier listening seems to carry too much weight compared with my latest choices of Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest Tool selection matters especially right now: I want to explore more music with that combination of weight, rhythmic complexity, and immersion.",
    "My repeated selections of Colony, Reroute to Remain, and Soundtrack to Your Escape suggest a sustained interest in heavier music that deserves more attention than a loose connection through catchy hooks."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in Tool and melodic punk, but stretch my broader rock listening beyond the heavier sound I want today."
}"}
